<h1>CSS for non-wrapping text</h1>

<p>Websites often have a maximum paragraph width, as long lines can be hard to read. It's usually no issue to insert line breaks automatically, but some text, like the preformatted contents of a &lt;pre> element, are not supposed to be altered.</p>

<p
id='after_general_css'>Listed above are this page's CSS properties and values which define boxes around &lt;pre> elements and a maximum paragraph width.</p>

<p>We can display the non-wrapping text within a box that scrolls if necessary. It makes sense to limit the width of the box to <var>--max-text-width</var>, as all text will remain within the same column. The four &lt;pre> elements that follow are of class <q>a</q>.</p>

